    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "A pencil costs $\\$x$. A pen costs $\\$1$ more. Sam bought one pencil and one pen, paying $\\$1.10$. How much did the pencil cost? Hint: Not 10 cents!",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "5 cents.",
      "worked": "The pen costs $(x+1)$ dollars.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x+(x+1)&=1.10\\\\2x+1&=1.10\\\\2x&=0.10\\\\x&=0.05\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe pencil costs 5 cents. Check: the pen costs $\\$1.05$, and $\\$0.05+\\$1.05=\\$1.10$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
